Z||000004||BC-GT||11-20-2001||11:34 AM||||Well, I'm not positive but, I've got a 85GT here and a decklid off a 88 Formula in my living room and the wiring inside them is different(different connections) Have not looked further into it though. both cars have remote trunk latches from factory. Bought the decklid because it had a wing attached to it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Zoom88||11-20-2001||12:43 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>what year......</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Trying to find out if there is a wire running to the rear deck coming off the switch in front. It uses a single wire to the solenoid. The wiring and connector for the switch are there, hav e even connected the switch to it already.<P>[This message has been edited by Zoom88 (edited 11-20-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Zoom88 (edited 11-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||11-20-2001||07:07 PM||||the 85 I'm told used a differant layout... So you don't have the correct wires even if you salvaged them.<P>in the 88, look at the connector that plugs into the deck lid. The lid you have has 3 wires but the car side has 4. the 4th wire goes to the latch. the latch grounds to the strike.<P>You'll need to pull the harness out of the lid to get the 4th wire installed. the directions for that are in my cave. You'll also need to buy a weather pack terminal and seal to crimp onto the new wire. You can get that at many parts stores. (see the wire service article in my cave for info on Weather Pack.)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||11-20-2001||08:35 PM||||I put an 85 solenoid on my Formula. I just snaked an additional wire down through the deck lid and tied it into the terminal block as described above||||reg||1
